  "script": "Another one from the family history books. In 1945, a man named Ebb Cade was badly hurt in a car crash in Tennessee. He was taken to a hospital at Oak Ridge. Doctors there injected him with plutonium without telling him, to see how it moved through the human body. He wasn't the only one. Eighteen people were injected in those studies. Fifty years later, a presidential committee investigated, and the President apologised. Read the file. Then ask who else never got told."
